  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 149 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nQuieter and much drier weather arrives today as winds pick up \nfrom the north. Gusts up to 20 to 25 mph at times will help usher \nin a dry and sunny day as high pressure moves into the region. \nTemperatures are expected to remain near or above normal today \nbefore warm air advection again increases through the middle of \nthe week. High temperatures on Thursday could get back towards the\nmiddle to upper 80s and maybe even low 90s, which could produce a\nfew sporadic showers in the afternoon. Still, no widespread \nactive weather is expected until sometime Thursday night into \nFriday with the next frontal passage. Rain and storms then stick \naround Friday into early Saturday before some quieter conditions \nreturn for the latter half of the weekend.",
